   ],
   "axis": "noncombat",
   "vs_three": "Comet Storm multikicked twice names all three opponents and Azula copies it (2X to each); Horizon Stone stores colorless mana between turns so X reaches 8 to 12, and the loops of the third route make X as large as needed; Mystical Teachings and Solve the Equation fetch it; Electrodominance copied adds 2X to one or two players plus two free spells. Recast for free an X spell has X=0: never do that. None of it needs combat damage through blockers."
  },
  "Azula and her copies in combat": {
   "cards": [
    "Fire Lord Azula",
    "Ozai, the Phoenix King",
    "Helm of the Host",
    "Godo, Bandit Warlord",
    "Overpowering Attack"
   ],
   "axis": "combat",
   "vs_three": "Overpowering Attack (freerunning {2}{R} once Azula has dealt combat damage) and Godo give extra combats, each a new firebending and a new round of copies; Helm of the Host makes a hasty nonlegendary Azula every combat, so two or three Azulas attack different opponents; Godo with Helm gives unlimited combats WITHOUT Azula (two-card late line, the route's redundancy when she is answered); Ozai (7/7 trample, haste, flying and indestructible with six floating mana) hits another player; copied pump tricks and removal after blocks make blocking a losing trade."
  },
  "Azula loops for unbounded mana": {
   "cards": [
    "Narset's Reversal",
    "Frantic Search",
    "Dualcaster Mage",
    "Snap",
    "Thermo-Alchemist"
   ],
   "axis": "noncombat",
   "vs_three": "While Azula attacks: (a) Dualcaster Mage plus Snap: Snap stays on the stack, each Dualcaster cast is copied, both bodies copy Snap, four lands untap for a 3-mana spell: unbounded mana and Dualcaster tokens; (b) Frantic Search plus Narset's Reversal (the Reversal's copy returns the Reversal itself, its copy returns Frantic Search): +1 mana per loop, +3 with the two reducers, about a dozen loops before the library runs low (never loop with Archmage Emeritus out: it decks you). Thermo-Alchemist untaps on each cast of loop (b) and pings all three opponents twice per loop; the unbounded mana of (a) goes into Comet Storm with X and kicks for all three. Mystical Teachings and Solve the Equation fetch every loop piece."
  }
